  "texts": {
    "preamble": "S.Muralidharan vs The Commissioner on 2 March, 2026 Author: R.Suresh Kumar Bench: R. Suresh Kumar Wp No. 6642 of 2026 In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated: 02-03-2026 Coram The Hon'Ble Mr.Manindra Mohan Shrivastava, Chief Justice And The Hon'Ble Mr Justice R. Suresh Kumar Wp No. 6642 of 2026 And Wmp No. 7215 Of 2026 S.Muralidharan Founder Indian Centre for Animal Rights and Education (Incare), S/o. Mr. P. Sivalingam, F1, No.40, R.S. Sridhar Street, Kottur, Chennai-600 085 ..Petitioner Vs 1. The Commissioner Greater chennai corporation Ripon Buildings, Chennai-600 003. 2.",
    "facts": "The relief sought by the petitioner is to direct the respondents to strictly enforce the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals (Slaughter House) Rules, 2001, Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 and allied laws to exercise statutory powers of inspection, licensing and enforcement against retail meat outlets carrying out illegal slaughter within Chennai District, and take action against illegal slaughter without mandatory veterinary supervision and humane stunning methods, ensure scientific lawful disposal of animal waste and file a detailed compliance and status report. 2. The entire petition does not contain any specific allegation against any particular shop or shops.",
